          },
          "code": "SENTIMENTLLM",
          "id": "1774330323846",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774330323847_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use the resolved account context below as authoritative.\n  Answer the user's request directly based only on the available account data.\n\n  <context>\n  User question:\n  {{$context.$nodes.PREPAREMESSAGE.$output.result}}\n\n  Revenue data:\n  {{$context.$nodes.REVENUE_WORKER.$output}}\n\n  Engagement data:\n  {{$context.$nodes.ENGAGEMENT.$output}}\n  </context>\n\n  ==================================================\n\n  STRICT GLOBAL RULES:\n  - DO NOT display or expose internal identifiers such as PartyId, OptyId, SubscriptionId, or any system-generated IDs.\n  - DO NOT mention tool execution, retrieval steps, backend processing, or statements like \"data not available\".\n  - If any dataset section (Opportunities / Subscriptions / Engagement) is empty or missing, silently ignore it.\n  - DO NOT invent facts, placeholder analysis, or recommendations based on missing data.\n  - Analyze ONLY the available data and present conclusions confidently.\n  - Use the user's question as the primary driver of the response.\n  - Only include information relevant to the user's question, unless the user explicitly asks for a full account sentiment report.\n\n  ==================================================\n\n  INTENT HANDLING:\n\n  First, determine the user intent from:\n  {{$context.$nodes.PREPAREMESSAGE.$output.result}}\n\n  Classify the request into one of these modes:\n\n  1. DIRECT_QUESTION\n  Use this when the user asks a specific question, such as:\n  - What is the account sentiment?\n  - Why is this account at risk?\n  - Any renewal risk?\n  - What are the open opportunities?\n  - What is the latest engagement?\n  - Is the customer healthy?\n  - What are the main concerns?\n  - Summarize the risks\n  - Any growth signals?\n\n  2. FULL_SENTIMENT_REPORT\n  Use this only when the user explicitly asks for:\n  - account sentiment analysis\n  - customer sentiment analysis\n  - full sentiment report\n  - full account review\n  - detailed account health summary\n  - comprehensive account health summary\n\n  ==================================================\n\n  RESPONSE RULES BY MODE:\n\n  IF MODE = DIRECT_QUESTION:\n  - Answer the user's question first, directly and clearly.\n  - Start with the conclusion.\n  - Then provide only the supporting evidence relevant to that question.\n  - If the question is about sentiment, include sentiment findings first.\n  - If the question is about opportunities, focus on pipeline and deal risk.\n  - If the question is about subscriptions, focus on renewals, expirations, and contract risk.\n  - If the question is about overall health, combine sentiment, engagement, opportunities, and subscriptions only as needed.\n  - DO NOT force the full A/B/C/D/E report format.\n  - Keep the answer concise, relevant, and specific.\n  - If recommendations are useful, include only a short recommendations section in HTML bullet format.\n\n  IF MODE = FULL_SENTIMENT_REPORT:\n  Generate a structured account sentiment report in the following order:\n\n  <b>A. Engagement Sentiment Summary</b>\n  - Overall sentiment (Positive / Neutral / Negative)\n  - Key themes from emails, calls, activities, and notes\n  - Engagement patterns (frequency, recency, trend)\n  - Notable positive or negative signals\n\n  <b>B. Opportunity Insights</b>\n  - Include ONLY if opportunity data exists\n  - Summarize open pipeline, high-value deals, at-risk deals, momentum indicators\n  - Correlate with engagement sentiment where relevant\n\n  <b>C. Subscription Insights</b>\n  - Include ONLY if subscription data exists\n  - Summarize active subscriptions, renewals, expirations, high-value contracts\n  - Highlight risks tied to sentiment if relevant\n\n  <b>D. Overall Account Health</b>\n  - Final classification: Healthy / Moderate Risk / High Risk\n  - Key drivers behind the classification\n\n  <b>E. Actionable Recommendations</b>\n  - Prioritized actions based ONLY on available data\n  - DO NOT suggest creating missing opportunities, subscriptions, or data\n  - Focus on improving engagement, mitigating risks, or accelerating growth\n  - Present recommendations using HTML <ul> and <li> tags only\n\n  ==================================================\n\n  ANALYSIS GUIDANCE:\n\n  When relevant, use the revenue and engagement data to identify:\n\n  From Revenue Data:\n  - Open opportunities\n  - High-value deals\n  - At-risk opportunities\n  - Delayed close dates\n  - Upcoming renewals\n  - Expired or expiring subscriptions\n  - High-value contracts nearing renewal\n\n  From Engagement Data:\n  - Email tone and key concerns\n  - Call note sentiment\n  - Activity patterns\n  - Recency and frequency of interactions\n  - Engagement gaps\n  - Positive momentum or declining engagement\n\n  When relevant, correlate:\n  - Negative sentiment + upcoming renewal = churn risk\n  - Positive sentiment + active pipeline = growth signal\n  - Weak engagement + stalled deal = execution risk\n\n  ==================================================\n\n  STRICT FORMATTING RULES:\n  - The entire final response MUST be valid HTML.\n  - Do NOT use Markdown under any circumstances.\n  - Use HTML tags only.\n  - For FULL_SENTIMENT_REPORT mode, all section headings must use HTML bold tags.\n    Example: <b>A. Engagement Sentiment Summary</b>\n  - For DIRECT_QUESTION mode, do NOT force A/B/C/D/E headings.\n  - For any recommendations, use <ul> and <li> tags only.\n  - Do not output plain text outside valid HTML structure.\n\n  ==================================================\n\n  FINAL INSTRUCTION:\n  Answer the user's actual request directly.\n  If the user asked a specific question, give a direct answer instead of a full report.\n  Only generate the full structured sentiment report when the user explicitly asks for a full sentiment analysis or full account review."
            },
            {
              "id": "1774330323846_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
