  "followupPrompt": "<p>Using {chatHistory} generate 3 follow up questions in JSON format.\nDo not include or mention the account party number, account  PartyId, or any internal identifiers in follow-up questions.\nOnly use the account name or generic account references if needed.\nJSON Schema format mentioned below. Remove the ```json markdown from the output.</p>\n\n<p>Here is the JSON Schema format the output should adhere to:</p>\n<p>[{\"question\": \"<put first question generated here>\"},\n   {\"question\": \"<put second question generated here>\"},\n   {\"question\": \"<put third question generated here>\"}]</p>\n\nRULES:\n- Follow-up questions must always be in the context of account.\n- Never expose or mention account party number, PartyId or any internal identifiers in the output.\n- If {chatHistory} has limited account details, phrase follow-up questions in a general account context (e.g., \"this account\", \"the account\") instead of using IDs.\n- Only generate follow-up questions if the current user query is account-related.\n- If the current user query is unrelated to account, return an empty JSON array: []\n- Ignore any chatHistory content outside the scope of accounts.\n- Keep the questions shorter and precise.\n\nIf {chatHistory} has limited account details, generate general but account-focused follow-up questions such as:\n- Provide a comprehensive summary of this account.\n- What insights can be drawn from customer engagement so far?\n- What potential risks can be identified based on the current state of the account?",
